{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3524","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3524","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3524\",\"parent_revision\":\"6c782b77e4a4b7104f7d857da14df4db7fb1a672ee35c6544c646bbe59e6e435\",\"root_revision\":\"6c782b77e4a4b7104f7d857da14df4db7fb1a672ee35c6544c646bbe59e6e435\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-09-13\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nRelated to but distinct from #3522. #3522 is a wiring defect \u2014 the `research-backlink-detector` agent is documented as owner of reciprocal rows but never spawned. This item is about the *output quality* of the shared transform both that agent and the validator's repair path call. Fixing #3522 without fixing this would wire up a generator of bad rows.\\n\\n`transform_to_backlink_description()` in `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/backlink_lib.py` is the single source of truth for the reciprocal-relationship phrase written into a cited entry by `validate_research.py check-backlinks --fix` and by `research-backlink-detector`. On PR #3510 it produced rows failing the bar its own governing document sets.\\n\\nObserved, repairing 8 asymmetric edges originating from `research/code-auditing/skylos.md`:\\n\\n1. Generic output. Five of eight rows came back as \\\"referenced by skylos (code-auditing)\\\" or \\\"is complemented by skylos (code-auditing)\\\". `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/cross-reference-format.md` states: \\\"The Relationship column names the specific conceptual link between the two entries. A generic label \u2014 'related tool', 'similar project', 'see also' \u2014 fails this bar.\\\" These rows carry no conceptual link; they restate the category, which already has its own column.\\n\\n2. A factually false assertion plus a broken sentence. The forward phrase \\\"provides AST graph context and dead-code analysis through MCP\\\" became \\\"consumes AST graph context and dead-code analysis through MCP provided by\\\". The verb inversion asserted that Skylos consumes CodeGraphContext's MCP output \u2014 an integration that does not exist; Skylos's documented MCP-facing commands are `verify_change` and `verify_agent`. The trailing \\\"provided by\\\" is a dangling fragment with no object.\\n\\nImpact. `check-backlinks` reports 823 asymmetric pairs vault-wide. Running `--fix` across them would generate this class of row at that scale, written into cited entries rather than the entry under review \u2014 so the defect lands in files nobody is reviewing. Mode (2) is the more serious: an inverted verb can manufacture a relationship claim no source supports, which is precisely the defect class the entry review rubric's gate 4 exists to catch.\\n\\nReproduction: on a research entry whose forward Cross-References row uses a directional verb (\\\"provides\\\", \\\"supplies\\\", \\\"extends\\\"), run `uv run --script .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py check-backlinks ./research --fix` and read the row written into the cited entry.\\n\\nObservations bounding the fix: the transform is deterministic with an INVERSE_VERBS mapping, so the failure is not randomness. Two distinct modes: (a) it falls back to a category-restating template when no verb matches, and (b) its verb inversion does not check whether inverting the verb preserves the truth of the claim. `cross-reference-format.md` explicitly designates this function as the single source of truth and instructs agents not to duplicate or inline the table, so the fix belongs in the library, not in the agents or the rubric.\\n\\nUser-provided context: PR #3510 hand-wrote all seven affected phrases rather than changing the library mid-research-PR. Those rows (in `hound.md`, `snyk-cli-cpp-scans.md`, `syft.md`, `merly-mentor.md`, `codegraphcontext.md`, `narsil-mcp.md`, `agent-skills-eval.md` as of commit fa865083f) are a usable reference for what acceptable output looks like.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: PR #3510 review (Codex threads on research/mcp-ecosystem/codegraphcontext.md and research/ai-research-tools/merly-mentor.md)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-13\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"bd9db6b82dac0d98d1637dca83e8628dda14045bf56bca735ee25e78f70b1065\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUPu3Lw\"}"}